# arts.kb — literature, music, the visual arts, architecture, theatre, film and dance.
#
# society.kb carries one line each for "art", "music", "literature", "painting", "theatre" and
# "film", which is enough to place them in the taxonomy and nothing like enough to answer a
# question about any of them. This file is the depth behind those six lines: the forms, the
# instruments, the movements, and the named works that are the usual currency of general
# knowledge.
#
# Two rules the rest of the KB already follows and that matter more here than elsewhere. Named
# works take `author` (functional — one value), so a work with a disputed author is left out
# rather than given a guess. And a movement is `is_a=art movement`, never `is_a` the medium it
# worked in, because a member of a movement is not a kind of painting.

# --- the arts, and what separates them ------------------------------------------------------- #
fine art | is_a=art | has_kind=painting | has_kind=sculpture | has_kind=drawing | has_kind=printmaking | purpose=making something to be contemplated rather than used
performing art | is_a=art | has_kind=music | has_kind=theatre | has_kind=dance | has_kind=opera | has_property=performed in front of an audience | requires=a performer
applied art | is_a=art | has_kind=architecture | has_kind=pottery | has_kind=calligraphy | means=art made for objects that are also used
aesthetics | is_a=branch of philosophy | involves=beauty | involves=taste | involves=what makes a work good
patron | is_a=person | purpose=paying for a work of art to be made | causes=art that would not otherwise exist
canon | is_a=collection of works | means=the works a tradition treats as its standard
masterpiece | is_a=work of art | means=a work regarded as the finest of its kind

# --- literature: the forms ------------------------------------------------------------------- #
literature | has_kind=fiction | has_kind=non-fiction | consists_of=written language
fiction | is_a=literature | means=narrative writing about invented people and events | has_kind=novel | has_kind=short story | has_kind=novella
non-fiction | is_a=literature | means=writing that presents itself as an account of real events | has_kind=biography | has_kind=essay | has_kind=history writing
novel | is_a=work of fiction | has_property=book length | has_part=plot | has_part=character | has_part=setting | has_kind=novel of manners | has_kind=detective novel
short story | is_a=work of fiction | has_property=readable at one sitting | has_property=a single main effect
novella | is_a=work of fiction | means=a story longer than a short story and shorter than a novel
poetry | is_a=literature | has_kind=epic | has_kind=lyric | has_kind=sonnet | has_kind=haiku | has_kind=free verse | involves=poetic metre
epic | is_a=poem | has_property=long | involves=a hero | involves=events on which a people's fate turns
lyric poem | is_a=poem | means=a short poem that speaks a single speaker's feeling
sonnet | is_a=poem | has_property=fourteen lines | involves=a fixed rhyme scheme | has_kind=Petrarchan sonnet | has_kind=Shakespearean sonnet
haiku | is_a=poem | has_property=three lines | has_property=seventeen syllables in Japanese | involves=a season word | birthplace=Japan
free verse | is_a=poem | means=poetry written without a regular metre or rhyme scheme
poetic metre | is_a=property of verse | means=the regular pattern of stressed and unstressed syllables in a line
rhyme | is_a=property of verse | means=a match between the end sounds of two words
stanza | is_a=part of a poem | means=a group of lines set off from the rest
drama | is_a=literature | purpose=being performed by actors | has_kind=tragedy | has_kind=comedy | has_part=dialogue | has_part=act
tragedy | is_a=drama | involves=a protagonist brought down | causes=pity in the audience | causes=fear in the audience
comedy | is_a=drama | has_property=ending happily | purpose=provoking laughter
essay | is_a=work of non-fiction | means=a short piece arguing or reflecting on one subject
biography | is_a=work of non-fiction | means=an account of one person's life written by someone else
autobiography | is_a=work of non-fiction | means=an account of a person's life written by that person
plot | is_a=part of a narrative | means=the ordered events of a story and how one leads to the next
character | is_a=part of a narrative | means=a person represented in a work
narrator | is_a=part of a narrative | means=the voice that tells the story
protagonist | is_a=character | means=the character whose choices the story follows
antagonist | is_a=character | means=the character who stands against the protagonist
setting | is_a=part of a narrative | means=the time and place in which a story happens
theme | is_a=part of a work | means=the idea a work keeps returning to
genre | is_a=category of works | means=a kind of work with conventions its readers expect | has_kind=tragedy | has_kind=comedy | has_kind=romance | has_kind=satire
satire | is_a=genre | purpose=attacking a folly or vice through ridicule | involves=irony
irony | is_a=figure of speech | means=saying one thing while the situation says the opposite
allegory | is_a=literary device | means=a narrative whose surface events stand for something else

