Rabindranath Tagore | is_a=poet | is_a=Nobel laureate in Literature | birthplace=Calcutta
Chinua Achebe | is_a=novelist | birthplace=Nigeria
Gabriel Garcia Marquez | is_a=novelist | birthplace=Colombia
George Orwell | is_a=novelist | is_a=essayist
Miguel de Cervantes | is_a=novelist | birthplace=Spain
Geoffrey Chaucer | is_a=poet | birthplace=London
Nobel Prize in Literature | is_a=prize | purpose=recognising an author's body of work | located_in=Sweden

# --- music: the elements ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
music | is_a=performing art | consists_of=sound organised in time | has_part=timbre
melody | is_a=element of music | means=a sequence of notes heard as a single line
harmony | is_a=element of music | means=notes sounded together | involves=chords
rhythm | is_a=element of music | means=the pattern of durations in time | involves=beat
beat | is_a=element of rhythm | means=the regular pulse a listener taps to
tempo | is_a=property of music | means=how fast the beat goes | unit=beats per minute
timbre | is_a=element of music | means=what makes two instruments playing the same note sound different
pitch | is_a=property of a note | means=how high or low it sounds | requires=frequency
note | is_a=unit of music | has_property=a pitch | has_property=a duration
scale | is_a=set of notes | means=the notes a piece draws on, in order of pitch | has_kind=major scale | has_kind=minor scale | has_kind=pentatonic scale
chord | is_a=group of notes | means=three or more notes sounded together
octave | is_a=musical interval | means=the interval between one note and another at twice its frequency
musical key | is_a=property of a piece | means=the scale a piece is centred on
musical notation | is_a=writing system | purpose=recording music so it can be played again | has_part=staff | has_part=clef | has_part=note head
composer | is_a=person | purpose=writing music
orchestra conductor | is_a=person | purpose=directing an orchestra in performance

# --- music: instruments and ensembles --------------------------------------------------------- #
musical instrument | is_a=tool | purpose=producing musical sound | has_kind=string instrument | has_kind=wind instrument | has_kind=percussion instrument | has_kind=keyboard instrument
string instrument | is_a=musical instrument | has_kind=violin | has_kind=guitar | has_kind=sitar | has_kind=cello | requires=a vibrating string
wind instrument | is_a=musical instrument | has_kind=flute | has_kind=trumpet | has_kind=clarinet | requires=a vibrating column of air
percussion instrument | is_a=musical instrument | has_kind=drum | has_kind=tabla | has_kind=xylophone | requires=being struck
keyboard instrument | is_a=musical instrument | has_kind=piano | has_kind=organ | has_kind=harpsichord | has_part=keyboard
violin | is_a=string instrument | has_property=played with a bow | has_property=the highest pitched instrument of its family
guitar | is_a=string instrument | has_property=six strings on the common form | has_property=plucked or strummed
sitar | is_a=string instrument | located_in=India | has_property=sympathetic strings that ring without being played
piano | is_a=keyboard instrument | has_property=strings struck by hammers | inventor=Bartolomeo Cristofori
flute | is_a=wind instrument | has_property=played by blowing across an opening
trumpet | is_a=wind instrument | has_property=brass | has_part=valve
drum | is_a=percussion instrument | has_part=membrane | has_property=played by striking
tabla | is_a=percussion instrument | located_in=India | has_property=a pair of hand drums
orchestra | is_a=musical ensemble | has_part=string section | has_part=woodwind section | has_part=brass section | has_part=percussion section | requires=an orchestra conductor@0.8
choir | is_a=musical ensemble | consists_of=singers | has_part=soprano part | has_part=alto part | has_part=tenor part | has_part=bass part
band | is_a=musical ensemble | has_kind=rock band | has_kind=brass band | has_kind=jazz band

# --- music: forms and traditions -------------------------------------------------------------- #
symphony | is_a=musical work | purpose=being played by an orchestra | has_property=usually in four movements@0.8
opera | is_a=performing art | consists_of=drama sung throughout | requires=singers | requires=an orchestra | birthplace=Italy
concerto | is_a=musical work | involves=a soloist set against an orchestra
sonata | is_a=musical work | purpose=being played by one or two instruments
song | is_a=musical work | consists_of=a melody set to words
classical music | is_a=musical tradition | has_kind=Western classical music | has_kind=Hindustani classical music | has_kind=Carnatic music
Hindustani classical music | is_a=classical music | located_in=northern India | involves=raga | involves=tala
Carnatic music | is_a=classical music | located_in=southern India | involves=raga | involves=tala
raga | is_a=melodic framework | located_in=India | means=a set of notes and rules for moving among them that gives a piece its mood
tala | is_a=rhythmic cycle | located_in=India | means=a repeating cycle of beats a piece is measured in
jazz | is_a=musical genre | birthplace=New Orleans | involves=improvisation | involves=syncopation
blues | is_a=musical genre | birthplace=the United States | involves=a twelve bar form@0.8 | causes=jazz@0.7
rock music | is_a=musical genre | involves=electric guitar | involves=a strong backbeat
folk music | is_a=musical genre | means=music passed on within a community rather than composed for publication
improvisation | is_a=musical practice | means=composing the music while performing it
Ludwig van Beethoven | is_a=composer | birthplace=Bonn | has_property=continued composing after going deaf
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart | is_a=composer | birthplace=Salzburg
Johann Sebastian Bach | is_a=composer | birthplace=Eisenach
Ravi Shankar | is_a=musician | birthplace=Varanasi | is_a=sitar player

# --- visual art ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
painting | is_a=fine art | has_kind=oil painting | has_kind=watercolour | has_kind=fresco | has_kind=mural
sculpture | is_a=fine art | means=art made as a three dimensional form | consists_of=stone | consists_of=bronze | consists_of=wood
drawing | is_a=fine art | requires=a mark making tool | has_kind=sketch
printmaking | is_a=fine art | means=making art by transferring ink from a prepared surface | has_kind=woodcut | has_kind=etching
photography | is_a=art form | requires=a camera | requires=light | inventor=Louis Daguerre
pigment | is_a=material | purpose=giving paint its colour | has_property=insoluble in the medium that carries it
canvas | is_a=material | purpose=providing a surface to paint on | consists_of=woven cloth
fresco | is_a=painting technique | means=painting onto wet plaster so the colour becomes part of the wall | requires=plaster
portrait | is_a=painting | means=a picture of a particular person
landscape | is_a=painting | means=a picture whose subject is the land itself
still life | is_a=painting | means=a picture of arranged inanimate objects
perspective | is_a=technique | purpose=making a flat picture read as depth | involves=a vanishing point
composition | is_a=property of a picture | means=how the parts of a work are arranged within it
art movement | is_a=category | means=a group of artists working from a shared aim in one period | has_kind=Renaissance art | has_kind=Impressionism | has_kind=Cubism | has_kind=Surrealism
Impressionism | is_a=art movement | located_in=France | involves=painting the effect of light | has_property=visible brushstrokes
Cubism | is_a=art movement | involves=showing a subject from several viewpoints at once
Surrealism | is_a=art movement | involves=images drawn from dreams and the unconscious
Renaissance art | is_a=art movement | located_in=Italy | involves=perspective | involves=the study of classical antiquity
Vincent van Gogh | is_a=painter | birthplace=the Netherlands | is_a=post-impressionist
Pablo Picasso | is_a=painter | birthplace=Malaga | is_a=cubist
Claude Monet | is_a=painter | birthplace=Paris | is_a=impressionist
Michelangelo | is_a=sculptor | is_a=painter | birthplace=Italy
Sistine Chapel ceiling | is_a=fresco | located_in=Vatican City | author=Michelangelo
Starry Night | is_a=painting | author=Vincent van Gogh
gallery | is_a=building | purpose=showing works of art
Louvre | is_a=museum | located_in=Paris | has_part=Mona Lisa

# --- architecture ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ #
architecture | is_a=applied art | purpose=designing buildings | involves=structure | involves=use | involves=appearance
architect | is_a=person | purpose=designing a building and overseeing its construction
column | is_a=structural element | purpose=carrying a load downward | has_kind=Doric column | has_kind=Ionic column | has_kind=Corinthian column
arch | is_a=structural element | purpose=spanning an opening | has_property=carries load into compression | causes=a span wider than one stone
dome | is_a=structural element | means=an arch rotated about its axis | purpose=roofing a wide space without internal supports
vault | is_a=structural element | means=an arched ceiling of stone or brick
buttress | is_a=structural element | purpose=resisting the outward push of an arch or vault
facade | is_a=part of a building | means=the face a building shows to the street
floor plan | is_a=drawing | means=a building seen in section from above
Gothic architecture | is_a=architectural style | involves=the pointed arch | involves=the flying buttress | involves=large stained glass windows | located_in=Europe
Classical architecture | is_a=architectural style | located_in=Ancient Greece | involves=the column | involves=symmetry
Mughal architecture | is_a=architectural style | located_in=India | involves=the dome | involves=inlaid stone
Taj Mahal | is_a=mausoleum | located_in=Agra | is_a=example of Mughal architecture | consists_of=white marble
Great Wall of China | is_a=fortification | located_in=China | purpose=defending a frontier
Colosseum | is_a=amphitheatre | located_in=Rome | purpose=holding public spectacles
Pyramids of Giza | is_a=tomb | located_in=Egypt | consists_of=stone

# --- theatre, dance and film -------------------------------------------------------------------- #
theatre | is_a=performing art | requires=actors | requires=an audience | has_part=script
actor | is_a=person | purpose=performing a role in front of an audience
theatre script | is_a=document | purpose=setting down what a play's characters say and do | has_part=dialogue | has_part=stage direction
stage | is_a=part of a theatre | purpose=giving the performance a place the audience can see
rehearsal | is_a=activity | purpose=preparing a performance before it is given | causes=a performance that holds together
dance | is_a=performing art | consists_of=movement organised in time | has_kind=ballet | has_kind=folk dance | has_kind=Bharatanatyam | has_kind=Kathak
ballet | is_a=dance | birthplace=Europe | has_property=a codified vocabulary of positions
Bharatanatyam | is_a=classical dance | located_in=southern India | involves=hand gestures | involves=facial expression
Kathak | is_a=classical dance | located_in=northern India | involves=rapid footwork | involves=spinning
film | consists_of=moving images | requires=a camera | has_part=scene | has_part=shot | has_kind=documentary | has_kind=animation
cinema | is_a=building | purpose=showing films to an audience
director | is_a=person | purpose=deciding how a film or play is performed
screenplay | is_a=document | purpose=setting down a film before it is shot
documentary | is_a=film | means=a film that presents itself as a record of real events
animation | is_a=film | means=film made from a sequence of drawn or modelled images | requires=many images per second
Bollywood | is_a=film industry | located_in=Mumbai | has_property=Hindi language films
